Maintainer: Mohammad Bisam Ali Aslam <mohammadbisamaliaslam@gmail.com>
Description: 
    A publication-grade Monte Carlo scenario-based pharmacoeconomic decision-analytic
    model for evaluating therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM)-guided palbociclib dosing
    in patients with hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative (HR+/HER2-) metastatic
    breast cancer.

    MODEL ARCHITECTURE:
    The package implements a two-component model:
    (1) A mechanistic one-compartment population pharmacokinetic model using
        literature-verified parameters (Royer et al. 2021, PMID:33668400;
        CL/F = 58.3 L/h, V/F = 1580 L, IIV 31.3%), producing a simulated mean
        Cmin of 70 ng/mL consistent with the published clinical median of 74.1 ng/mL
        (Leenhardt et al. 2022, PMID:35456675).
    (2) A scenario-based risk assignment framework calibrated to PALOMA-2 trial
        outcomes (baseline G3/4 neutropenia 66.4%; Finn et al. 2016, PMID:27959613)
        and Leenhardt et al. 2022 TDM intervention data (NNT = 6.3, PMID:35397465).
        This approach is appropriate given the near-flat Emax exposure-toxicity
        curve (gamma = 0.13; Courlet et al. 2022, PMID:35890213), which precludes
        mechanistic risk discrimination across the therapeutic Cmin range.

    PHARMACODYNAMIC MODEL:
    Simplified sigmoidal Emax approximation calibrated to Courlet et al. 2022:
    E0 = 0.66, Emax = 0.22, EC50 = 40.1 ng/mL, gamma = 0.13.
    Unit-verified: all outputs on valid probability scale (0-1).

    TDM DECISION ALGORITHM:
    Five-tier Cmin classification system (Leenhardt et al. 2022, PMID:35397465):
    Tier 1 (<40 ng/mL): evaluate; Tier 2 (40-70): continue;
    Tier 3 (70-100): optimal★; Tier 4 (100-150): reduce to 100 mg;
    Tier 5 (>150): reduce/hold. TDM threshold: 100 ng/mL.

    KEY FINDINGS (n = 1,000 virtual patients, seed = 12345):
    - Simulated mean Cmin:             70.0 ng/mL (literature: 74.1 ng/mL)
    - Baseline Grade 3/4 neutropenia:  66.0% (PALOMA-2 target: 66.4%)
    - TDM-guided G3/4 risk:            50.4%
    - Absolute Risk Reduction (ARR):   15.6%
    - Number Needed to Treat (NNT):    6.4 (Leenhardt 2022 observed: 6.3)
    - Cases prevented per 1,000:       156 annually
    - Dose modification rate:          36.4% (PALOMA-2: 36.4%)
    - Gross AE savings (1,000 pts):    $3,563,045
    - TDM programme cost (1,000 pts):  $350,000 ($350/patient, LC-MS/MS)
    - Net savings (1,000 patients):    $3,213,045 annually
    - Savings per patient:             $3,213
    - ROI on TDM investment:           918%
    - Cost per case prevented:         NEGATIVE (net cost-saving)

    SENSITIVITY ANALYSIS:
    One-way sensitivity analysis (6 parameters) and two-way sensitivity analysis
    (hospitalization cost $11,337-$35,899 x ARR 8-24%; 10x10 = 100 scenarios).
    Break-even ARR = 1.5% at base hospitalization cost ($22,839).
    TDM cost-saving in 100% of two-way SA scenarios tested.
    All sensitivity values computed analytically — nothing hardcoded.

    THREE-TIER VALIDATION FRAMEWORK:
    Tier 1 (PK distribution): simulated Cmin consistent with Leenhardt 2022 (PASS).
    Tier 2 (scenario calibration): baseline risk and NNT within pre-specified
    tolerance of published targets (PASS).
    Tier 3 (cross-source PK): MAPE = 6.8% across 5 independent sources (PASS).
    9/9 validation tests passed.

    COST MODEL:
    Hospitalization cost: $22,839 (Dulisse & Cosler 2012, PMC3440789), applied
    as a probability-weighted composite expected value representing the management
    burden of Grade 3/4 neutropenia (outpatient + hospitalised subset).
    Sensitivity range: $11,337 (Kuderer 2015 ASH, breast-specific) to $35,899
    (Flanigan et al. 2024, PMID:38777864, most recent real-world estimate).



    WORKFLOW (run in order):
    1. src/01_model_setup.R        — Single source of truth for all parameters;
                                     integrity checks; master parameter table
    2. src/02_simulation_engine.R  — Monte Carlo scenario model; PK distribution;
                                     scenario risk assignment; economic outcomes
    3. src/03_sensitivity_analysis.R — One-way (tornado) + two-way (heatmap)
                                     sensitivity analysis; break-even analysis
    4. src/04_report_generator.R   — Markdown report; paste-ready Results section
    5. src/05_data_import.R        — PALOMA trial reference data; PK literature;
                                     AE costs; validation cohort (Leenhardt 2022)
    6. src/06_validation.R         — Three-tier validation framework; 4-panel figure
    7. src/07_tdm_algorithm.R      — 5-tier Cmin classification; decision function;
                                     exposure-response figures; tier distribution
    8. src/08_cost_visualisation.R — Cost breakdown; waterfall; budget impact;
                                     NNT infographic; 4-panel economic summary
   

    REPRODUCIBILITY:
    All stochastic outputs use set.seed(12345). Parameters saved to
    data/parameters.RData as single source of truth. All sensitivity
    values computed from formula — nothing hardcoded. Base R only
    (no tidyverse dependency in core scripts).

